PART 8 — STRICT ORDER RESULT AND WINDOW CLEANUP

THIS IS ONE OF THE MOST IMPORTANT REQUIREMENTS IN THE ENTIRE PROJECT.

The automation must never leave an order parameters window or execution-result window blocking the terminal after a trade attempt.

This must be guaranteed for MT4 and MT5.

The terminal's order form is a blocking interface. While it is open, the automation may be unable to search for another symbol, interact with Market Watch, right-click a row or open another order.

A click on Buy or Sell is not proof that a trade was successful.

The broker needs time to process the request and return its actual response.

Required sequence after every submission

Submit the order exactly once.

Enter a processing/waiting state.

Poll the terminal for the actual broker response.

Detect a successful execution, a definitive rejection or an unknown outcome.

Record the result.

Locate the result window or notification.

Click its actual OK button when present.

Wait for the dismissal to complete.

Verify that the result window is no longer visible.

Verify that any blocking order form has been closed or safely dismissed.

Confirm that the terminal is ready for another order.

A short delay after clicking OK is not sufficient proof that the dialog has disappeared. Confirm its absence through the DOM.

Success response

For a successful trade:

Identify the broker's completion/result message.

Record the execution result.

Find the corresponding OK button inside the correct result dialog.

Click OK.

Wait for the result dialog to disappear.

Verify that the terminal is interactive again.

Continue to the next authorized order if required.

Rejected trade

Examples include:

